  "story": "Snowballs roll along a narrow path, all at the same speed. A positive number is a ball of that size rolling right; a negative number is a ball rolling left, with the size written without the minus. When a right-roller meets a left-roller the smaller one breaks, and equal sizes both break. Balls rolling the same way never meet. How many balls are left when all the meetings are over?",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "balls", "type": "array<num>"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 0, "max": 1000},
    "notes": ["Sizes are 1 to 100; no ball has size 0."]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.sub", "cmp.eq", "cmp.gt", "cmp.lt", "ctrl.else", "ctrl.foreach", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "ctrl.while", "lit.num", "logic.and", "logic.not", "new.stack", "stack.empty", "stack.peek", "stack.pop", "stack.push", "var.get", "var.inc", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 88
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 45550, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 100},
  "hints": ["Only a right-roller followed later by a left-roller can meet, so keep the right-rollers still in play on a stack.", "A left-roller smashes smaller right-rollers from the top of the stack one after another (WHILE), until it meets a bigger or equal one or the stack is empty.", "Equal sizes break each other; a left-roller that clears the stack rolls away safely and counts. The balls left on the stack count too."],
